    "summary": "DaemonWorkerInit gained a required lockBlock beside guardBlock, and startDaemonWorker installs it with installLockManager, so every daemon worker shares the main thread's named locks. The worker-stores test and its helper worker pass a lock block; the helper gained a lock-probe op, and a new test shows a daemon worker refused (with the main thread named as holder) while the main thread holds the lock shared, then granted after release. Checked by hand: tsc --noEmit rejects a startDaemonWorker call without lockBlock (TS2345 'Property lockBlock is missing'), using a temporary probe file under src/daemon/threads that was then removed (tsc excludes __tests__, so the test callers themselves are not typechecked); removing the install line makes the contention test fail.",
